# ============================================================
# Lesson 01 — say
#
# Keyword of this lesson: say
#
# Run it:
#     python3 juru.py examples/guide/01_say.jr
#
# say makes the computer show something to you. It is the
# simplest keyword in the language, and the one you will use
# the most.
# ============================================================

# Text goes out exactly as written:
say("JuRu talks to you")

# Numbers go out too — whole and decimal:
say(42)
say(3.5)

# The part inside say(...) is computed first, then printed:
say(2 + 2)
say(2 + 2 * 10)

# Pieces join with +. Text + number is converted for you:
say("the answer is " + 42)
say("a" + "b" + "c")

# And of course say works with variables:
name = "Ada"
say("Hello, " + name + "!")
